 bibliography=('Retained Wikipedia Russian grammar oldid1369617627, catalog/sources/units-26-30/wikipedia/russian-grammar-1369617627.txt, CC BY-SA 4.0 under retained FREEZE rights attestation: complete Adjectives introduction, long/short declension table and qualifications before Comparison of adjectives. '
  'Immutable admitted short-form capability sourceHash0b5b1bad657a8c901ba9f471ff7adff3a945be6f281aa760f58c59fd0f8c78e8 identifies the invariant beige and khaki forms, the supplied new long/short pair, and short forms in nominative/predicative use. '
  'Only the already admitted long new, short new and invariant beige forms are classified. Short adjectives vary for gender/number, not case; some adjectives lack short forms, and spelling/stress cannot be generated by a universal truncation rule. Long forms can also be predicates: do not infer an exceptionless word-position rule. '
  'Vocabulary glosses remain available as optional word-meaning practice and do not satisfy the grammar gate. Broader agreement and sentence-level predicate/attribute application remain pending. '
  'Independently authored English on 2026-10-13 within content-audit-2026-10-08; no new Russian forms, copied primary prose or private Penguin text; qualified semantic audit pending.')
 changes=[];added=[];pins={};newitems=[];voc='obj-u29-adjective-vocabulary'
 def record(value,name,original=None,applications=None,rid=None,target=None):
  target=target or obj
  original=original or bibliography+'\n'+value;r=deepcopy(template)
